          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em compact-open-topology
            is a natural
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+spaces"} mapping spaces
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+spaces"} locally compact topological spaces
            to be
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential+object"} exponentiable
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GivesExponentialObject"}
          %p
            The compact-open topology on the set of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Y
            is generated by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+of+a+topology"} subbasis
            of subsets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi U
                    %mi K
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U^K \subset C(X,Y)
            that map a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+subspace"} compact subspace
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \subset X
            to a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subset"} open subset
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \subset Y
          %p
            When restricting to continuous functions between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated topological spaces
            one usually modifies this definition to a subbase of open subsets
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi K
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U^{\phi(K)}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(K)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact topological space
            under any continuous function
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi K
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \colon K \to X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
            in the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated topological spaces
            (see also at
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convenient+category+of+topological+spaces"} convenient category of topological spaces
          %p
            The two definitions agree when the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+space"} compactly generated
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff space
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %p In the following we consider:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, \mathcal{O}_{X})
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Y, \mathcal{O}_{Y})
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Y
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y^{X}
                (also written
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Maps
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Maps(X,Y)
                or
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^0(X,Y)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+maps"} continuous maps
                from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\mathcal{O}_{X})
                to
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Y
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒪
                          %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Y, \mathcal{O}_{Y})
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mi X
                        %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}^{c}_{X}
                the set of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsets"} subsets
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                which are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+subset"} compact
                with respect to
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒪
                          %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_{X}
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi M
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mo ,
                          %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_{A,U}
                , for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∈
                      %msubsup
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mi X
                        %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \mathcal{O}^{c}_{X}
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒪
                          %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in \mathcal{O}_{Y}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \rightarrow Y
                such that
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(A) \subset U
          %p
          #CompactOpenTopology.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              The
              %em compact-open topology
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Y
                          %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_{Y^{X}}
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Y
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y^{X}
              is that with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+of+a+topological+space"} sub-basis
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi M
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mo ,
                          %mi U
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} |
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∈
                      %msubsup
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mi X
                        %mi c
                      %mo ,
                      %mi U
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mi Y
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Big\{M_{A,U} \,\Big\vert \, A \in \mathcal{O}^{c}_{X}, U \in \mathcal{O}_{Y}\Big\}
          %h2#Exponentiability Exponentiability
          %p
          #LocallyCompact.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, \mathcal{O}_{X})
              is
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+space"} locally compact
              if the set of compact neighbourhoods of points of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              form a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neighbourhood+basis"} neighbourhood basis
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              and every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neighbourhood"} neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ∈
                    %msubsup
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi X
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \in \mathcal{O}^{c}_{X}
              and a
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in \mathcal{O}_{X}
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi U
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi V
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in U \subset V \subset N
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              There are many variations on def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocallyCompact"}
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+space"} locally compact space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, \mathcal{O}_{X})
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff
              %em not
              however make the assumption that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, \mathcal{O}_{X})
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff
          #evIsContinuous.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, \mathcal{O}_{X})
              be a locally compact topological space, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocallyCompact"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Y, \mathcal{O}_{Y})
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ev
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi Y
                      %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ev : X \times Y^{X} \rightarrow Y
              given by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,f) \mapsto f(x)
              is continuous, where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi Y
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times Y^{X}
              is equipped with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topology"} product topology
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ×
                        %msup
                          %mi Y
                          %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_{X \times Y^{X}}
              with respect to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_{X}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Y
                          %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_{Y^{X}}
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CompactOpenTopology"}
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              By an elementary fact concerning continuous maps, it suffices to show that for any
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %msup
                        %mi Y
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,f) \in X \times Y^{X}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in \mathcal{O}_{Y}
              such that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) \in U
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ×
                        %msup
                          %mi Y
                          %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U' \in \mathcal{O}_{X \times Y^{X}}
              such that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi U
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,f) \in U'
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ev
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ev(U') \subset U
            %p To demonstrate this, we make the following observations.
            %p
              1) Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is continuous, we have that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}(U) \in \mathcal{O}_{X}
            %p
              2) Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, \mathcal{O}_{X})
              is locally compact, we deduce from 1) that there is a
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ∈
                    %msubsup
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi X
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \in \mathcal{O}^{c}_{X}
              and a
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ″
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U'' \in \mathcal{O}_{X}
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi U
                      %mo ″
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi V
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in U'' \subset V \subset f^{-1}(U)
            %p
              3) By 2) and by definition of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ×
                        %msup
                          %mi Y
                          %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_{X \times Y^{X}}
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi Y
                            %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_{Y^{X}}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ″
                      %mo ×
                      %msub
                        %mi M
                        %mrow
                          %mi V
                          %mo ,
                          %mi U
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mo ×
                          %msup
                            %mi Y
                            %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U'' \times M_{V, U} \in \mathcal{O}_{X \times Y^{X}}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi U
                      %mo ″
                      %mo ×
                      %msub
                        %mi M
                        %mrow
                          %mi V
                          %mo ,
                          %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,f) \in U'' \times M_{V, U}
            %p
              4) Let
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ,
                      %mi f
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi U
                      %mo ″
                      %mo ×
                      %msub
                        %mi M
                        %mrow
                          %mi V
                          %mo ,
                          %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x',f') \in U'' \times M_{V, U}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi U
                      %mo ″
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x' \in U''
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo ″
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi f
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f'(U'') \subset f'(V) \subset U
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi M
                        %mrow
                          %mi V
                          %mo ,
                          %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_{V, U}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f'(x) \in U
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ev
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo ″
                      %mo ×
                      %msub
                        %mi M
                        %mrow
                          %mi V
                          %mo ,
                          %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ev(U'' \times M_{ V, U}) \subset U
            %p
              By 3) and 4), we see that we can take
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
